<title>GERMANY: Wilhelmshaven oil refinery sold to Dreyfus - Director.</title>
<headline>Wilhelmshaven oil refinery sold to Dreyfus - Director.</headline>
<dateline>WILHELMSHAVEN 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankrupt BETA refinery in Wilhelmshaven has been sold to a company owned by the Hamburg based part of the Louis Dreyfus group, the managing director of the plant, Johan Anton van Weelden said.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale was decided on Thursday Feb 20 to Wilhelmshavener Raffineriegesellschaft mbH i.G., which is owned by Dreyfus,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
